---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/common/Header.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Cookie policy for BiblicalMeal - how we use cookies and tracking technologies."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="bg-background">
    <section class="container-site py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
        <p class="eyebrow text-terracotta">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-h1 text-ink">Cookie Policy</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink-muted">
          <em
            >Last updated: {
              new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
                year: 'numeric',
                month: 'long',
                day: 'numeric',
              })
            }</em
          >
        </p>

        <section class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-ink">What Are Cookies?</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink">
            Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a
            website. They help the site remember your preferences and understand
            how you use it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-ink">How We Use Cookies</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink">
            BiblicalMeal uses cookies minimally. Here's what we use:
          </p>

          <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink">Necessary Cookies</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                <strong>Status: None currently required.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                BiblicalMeal is a static website that does not currently require
                any cookies for basic functionality.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink">Analytics Cookies</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                <strong
                  >Status: Integration-ready (not currently active).</strong
                >
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                When you consent to analytics tracking, Google Analytics sets
                the following cookies:
              </p>
              <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-6 text-body text-ink-muted">
                <li class="mt-1">
                  <strong>_ga</strong> — Distinguishes unique users by assigning a
                  randomly generated number as a client identifier.
                </li>
                <li class="mt-1">
                  <strong>_ga_</strong> — Used to maintain session state.
                </li>
              </ul>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                These cookies are only set if you explicitly consent to
                analytics tracking. No tracking occurs without your consent.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink">Consent Storage</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                <strong>Status: Currently implemented.</strong>
              </p>
              <p class="mt-2 text-body text-ink-muted">
                We store your cookie consent preference in localStorage (not a
                cookie) under the key <code>bm-consent</code>. This remembers
                your choice so you don't have to choose again on each visit.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-ink">Your Choices</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink">You have control over cookies:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 text-body text-ink-muted">
            <li class="mt-2">
              <strong>Consent banner:</strong> When you first visit, you can accept
              or reject analytics cookies.
            </li>
            <li class="mt-2">
              <strong>Manage preferences:</strong> Click "Manage Preferences" in the
              cookie banner to change your choices at any time.
            </li>
            <li class="mt-2">
              <strong>Browser settings:</strong> You can block or delete cookies through
              your browser settings.
            </li>
            <li class="mt-2">
              <strong>Clear localStorage:</strong> You can clear the consent preference
              by clearing your browser's localStorage for this site.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-ink">Third-Party Cookies</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted">
            <strong>Currently implemented:</strong> None. BiblicalMeal does not currently
            use any third-party cookies.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted">
            <strong>Integration-ready:</strong> Google Analytics cookies (only if
            you consent to analytics tracking).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-12">
          <h2 class="font-display text-h2 text-ink">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted">
            We may update this cookie policy from time to time. Changes will be
            posted on this page with an updated date.
          </p>
        </section>

        <div class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-8">
          <p class="text-caption text-ink-muted">
            This cookie policy reflects the actual current behavior of the
            BiblicalMeal repository. We do not claim GDPR compliance or legal
            certification. This is a transparency document, not a legal
            guarantee.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
